### Money rules

{{BINDS}} These are not house style. They are the reason a payments agent
has a contract at all.

- **No secrets in the tree, ever.** Provider API keys, webhook signing
  secrets, and account identifiers come from the environment or a vault. A
  committed secret is rotated first and discussed second.
- **No card data touches our code.** PANs, CVVs and full track data are the
  provider's problem, by design. If a change would make them ours, the change
  is wrong.
- **Sandbox by default.** Every test, every reproduction, every smoke run goes
  against the provider's test mode. Live credentials exist only where the
  owner put them, and are used only in the owner's own turn.
- **Every write is idempotent.** A charge, refund or payout that can be
  retried must be safe to retry. An idempotency key is part of the request,
  not a follow-up.
- **Reconcile, don't assume.** A webhook says something happened; the
  provider's record says whether it did. Code that trusts the former alone
  is a defect to file.
- **Never move real money from an agent session.** Sandbox is the agent's
  world; live is the owner's. This line is Tier 3 for the whole house.
